20,2,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
21,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
22,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
23,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
24,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
25,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Transport costs vary wildly depending on distance. Public beds are cheap, but we must account for everything.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"Public bookings are a bureaucratic nightmare. Also, cooking for ourselves on campus is a huge burden on the staff.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Minako,,"It seems the evenings are key for bonding, but we're losing members who don't attend away camps.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Our own hall is overcrowded during vacation. Also, inland centers can be very cramped with strict rules.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"A third of us can't commute early. Also, whole-building lets are risky if people cancel last minute.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, if commuting is an issue, staying local might actually increase costs for beds.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, that's true. And if we go public, the application process is too rigid for our needs.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Jonathan, if the inland centers are too strict, will people actually relax and bond?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,Likely not. Poor sleep and rigid schedules would probably make the training sessions suffer.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, if the campus canteen is closed, we're back to the cooking problem you mentioned.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"We need a balance. A distant lodge is expensive for transport, but public centers are a lottery.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Toshio,,I agree. We can't have the organizers spending all their time on paperwork or cooking.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Minako,,"We need everyone in one place to fix the year-group divide, but it must be accessible.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,Campus seems impractical given the hall schedule and the commute for some members.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Asuka,,And the financial risk of a private lodge is high if the membership is unstable.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"Let's consider the options. We have the Coastal Lodge, Campus Intensive, or the Mountain Training Centre.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,4,talk,Toshio,,Campus is out because of the cooking and the hall timetable.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,4,talk,Minako,,"If we want the year-groups to mix, the Mountain Centre or Lodge are better than Campus.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,The Mountain Centre sounds too restrictive based on the reports I saw.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"The Lodge is risky, but the Mountain Centre is a lottery.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,3,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
46,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
47,3,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
